---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Roadmap — Skyhook Industries" description="A risk-driven development roadmap for Skyhook Industries, from reference architecture and materials through orbital demonstrations and momentum exchange.">
  <div class="shell">
    <section class="page-hero"><p class="eyebrow">Roadmap</p><h1>Engineering gates, not fictional deadlines.</h1><p>The original website attached calendar dates to increasingly large tethers before the underlying architecture had closed. The new roadmap advances when a measurable technical risk has been retired.</p></section>
    <section class="page-section">
      <div class="roadmap-step"><span class="step">01</span><div><h2>Reference architecture</h2><p>Close the first coherent model of orbit, tether length, mass distribution, rotation rate, rendezvous geometry, payload class, momentum transfer and reboost throughput. Publish assumptions and sensitivity ranges.</p></div></div>
      <div class="roadmap-step"><span class="step">02</span><div><h2>Materials and structural coupons</h2><p>Characterize specific strength, fatigue, joining, thermal cycling, radiation and atomic-oxygen exposure for candidate tether constructions. Validate redundant load paths rather than assuming ideal fibers.</p></div></div>
      <div class="roadmap-step"><span class="step">03</span><div><h2>Ground dynamics demonstrator</h2><p>Test deployment, rotation control, segmented construction, capture compliance and failure isolation at the smallest scale that can answer meaningful questions.</p></div></div>
      <div class="roadmap-step"><span class="step">04</span><div><h2>Subscale orbital tether</h2><p>Demonstrate deployment, tracking, long-duration dynamics, collision-avoidance operations and electrodynamic interaction in the intended operational environment.</p></div></div>
      <div class="roadmap-step"><span class="step">05</span><div><h2>Momentum-exchange demonstration</h2><p>Rendezvous with and capture a small free-flying payload, transfer a measurable amount of momentum, release predictably and quantify the resulting change to the tether's orbit.</p></div></div>
      <div class="roadmap-step"><span class="step">06</span><div><h2>Reusable transportation prototype</h2><p>Scale only after the preceding system demonstrates repeatability, survivability and a credible path to restoring momentum between missions.</p></div></div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
